After pausing that very lucky game[*] for a whole week I restarted
it today with my hero standing on the stairs in the entry chamber
of Moloch's Sanctum, still pondering whether I'd take the repeated
levelport shortcut, or fight my way through the graveyard. My tame
lich, meanwhile a high-level arch-lich[**], quietly jumping around
my feet.

I decided that one of the three magic lamps that I found shall now
be spent for a blessed spellbook of charm monster. I didn't expect
otherwise, got the spellbook. Though, suddenly, Yeenoghu appeared
out of thin air. I didn't worry much because he (it?) is covetous,
and, right, as fast as he popped up he disappeared from the room.

While I read the spellbook, only a couple turns later, Yeenoghu was
back. My spellbook studies still uninterrupted a battle between my
arch-lich and Yeenoghu took place. And a short time span later the
demon was dead and an amulet lying on the floor. I finished reading
my book, still standing on the stairs. Oh dear, what a hard task it
was to get that precious and well guarded Amulet!

The only problem now might be that my pet arch-lich, once again,
got confused during the fight with Yeenoghu. Shall I leave him back
in Moloch's Sanctum with all the other undead still around, or take
him with me, and suffering from his annoying attacks? Anyway..

One question I have; where did big Y came from? Has he inadvertently
be summoned by my own arch-lich while he was in my vicinity? (As far
as I know, Yeenoghu can only be summoned and will never be generated
as a random monster?)

And what kind of horrors will come next to support my game...?

Janis

